spes: reset to the bootloader, PMIC clock, two SIM slots, lock selector, later modem questions (0179).

1. bsd/dev/spes_pmic.c (new, boot-arg spespmic=1): sysctl debug.spes_reset resets the phone
   (1), to the bootloader (2) or to the recovery (3), as Linux msm-poweroff + qpnp-power-on do:
   reason in PON_SOFT_RB_SPARE, restart_reason cookie in IMEM, optional PS_HOLD type (0x10
   warm, 0x20 hard), PS_HOLD dropped. "reboot" over SSH hangs at "hfs: unmount initiated" and
   every forced reset costs a fastboot slot retry. sysctl hw.spes_rtc reads the PM6125 RTC
   counter: the clock starts at 1969 on every boot. PMIC writes: only 0x85a, 0x85b, 0x88f.
2. WWAN probe: wwan bit 3 (8) activates a GW provisioning session on each slot whose SIM/USIM
   is only "detected" (first primary, second secondary) and binds a second NAS client to
   subscription 2. With 0178 the modem went ONLINE by itself and showed a USIM in slot 2 as
   "detected", serving "searching" (live-k0177va-b2.txt).
3. WWAN probe: the first round is 10 s after the services appear and every round asks for the
   operating mode and the card status; the answers at 0.5 s (mode 5, no cards) were not final.
   16 rounds.
4. AppleKeyStore selector 8 (SpringBoard, at each lock) answered kIOReturnUnsupported in every
   boot; it now succeeds like the other lock/unlock selectors. Untested guess for the lock
   screen that stopped taking the swipe up after display off/on.

